IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-application`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 4 and 5. Expected values are worked out from the calendar and
-- the text, with the working beside each assertion.

§ `Regulations s 4 -- tests`

-- 4(2): an application the Minister has not received has not been made.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` NOTHING (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS NOTHING

-- 4(3): the applicant turns 18 on 10 May 2008; six months before that is 10 November 2007.
-- One day before the window: deemed received when it was received.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 11 9)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 11 9)
-- The first day of the window, a day in the middle, and the day before the birthday:
-- deemed received on the birthday.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2007 11 10)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 10)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 2 1)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 10)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 9)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 10)
-- On the birthday itself and after it: the day it was received.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 10)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 10)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 11)) (YearMonthDay 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 5 11)
-- A 31 August birthday: six months before is the last day of February (fork F14: the
-- month arithmetic clamps), 29 February 2008 in a leap year and 28 February 2009 otherwise.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 2 29)) (YearMonthDay 1990 8 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 8 31)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 2 28)) (YearMonthDay 1990 8 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2008 2 28)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 2 28)) (YearMonthDay 1991 8 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 8 31)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been made` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 2 27)) (YearMonthDay 1991 8 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 2 27)

-- 4(4): ceasing. A person who is a beneficiary and no longer meets the criteria of section
-- 2 stops receiving the allocation and must apply again; a person who is not a beneficiary
-- has nothing to cease; a month that is ineligible only because of a suspension the
-- beneficiary asked for does not cease the allocation (fork F11).
GIVEN filed IS A BOOLEAN
      susp  IS A MAYBE `Suspension at the beneficiary's request`
GIVETH A `Person facts for a month`
`a person in August 2025 whose return is` filed `and whose suspension is` susp MEANS
    `Person facts for a month` WITH
        `the month asked about`                       IS YearMonthDay 2025 8 15
        `date of birth`                               IS YearMonthDay 1990 5 10
        `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS TRUE
        `a Canadian citizen`                          IS TRUE
        `a permanent resident`                        IS FALSE
        `a temporary resident`                        IS FALSE
        `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS 0
        `a protected person`                          IS FALSE
        `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS FALSE
        `the custody under a sentence`                IS NOTHING
        `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS filed
        `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
        `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
        `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
        `the suspension the beneficiary asked for`    IS susp

`a suspension that began on 1 August 2025` MEANS `Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH
    `the day the suspension took effect` IS YearMonthDay 2025 8 1
    `a day in the month payment resumed` IS NOTHING

#ASSERT `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` TRUE (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE `and whose suspension is` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` TRUE (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` TRUE `and whose suspension is` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` FALSE (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE `and whose suspension is` NOTHING)
-- Suspended at the person's request for the whole month and otherwise eligible: not ceased,
-- although the person is not eligible for the month (s 2(6)).
#ASSERT NOT `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` TRUE (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` TRUE `and whose suspension is` (JUST `a suspension that began on 1 August 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` TRUE `and whose suspension is` (JUST `a suspension that began on 1 August 2025`))
-- Suspended and also failing a criterion: ceased.
#ASSERT `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` TRUE (`a person in August 2025 whose return is` FALSE `and whose suspension is` (JUST `a suspension that began on 1 August 2025`))

§ `Regulations s 5 -- tests`

-- 5(1): the earliest eligible day, when it falls after the 24-month floor.
-- Applied on 15 September 2025; the floor is 15 September 2023; eligible from 1 June 2025.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1)
-- 5(2): the 24-month floor, when the earliest eligible day is before it.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 15)
-- On either side of the floor: 14, 15 and 16 September 2023.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 14)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 15)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 15)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 15)
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 16)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 9 16)
-- The floor from a day that has no match 24 months back: 29 February 2028 less 24 months
-- is 28 February 2026 (clamped).
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2028 2 29) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
-- No day on which the applicant is eligible and unpaid: not approved.
#ASSERT `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 15) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
